---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Behavioral Psychology: what information this site collects, how cookies are used, and how to contact us."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <span>Privacy Policy</span></p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>How Behavioral Psychology handles your information. Last updated: November 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Behavioral Psychology (behavioralpsychology.pro) is an independent educational publication. This privacy policy explains what information is collected when you visit the site, how it is used, and what choices you have. The policy is written in plain language on purpose.</p>

        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>This is a static informational website. There are no user accounts, no comment system, no newsletter signup, and no forms that collect personal details. The site does not ask you to register, log in, or hand over your name, address, or payment information.</p>
        <p>The only personal information you might share with us is what you choose to include in an email. If you write to <a href="mailto:info@behavioralpsychology.pro">info@behavioralpsychology.pro</a>, your email address and the contents of your message are used only to read and respond to your message. We do not add email correspondents to any marketing list, and we do not share or sell email addresses.</p>

        <h2>Automatically Collected Information</h2>
        <p>Like most websites, the hosting infrastructure for this site records basic technical information in server logs: the pages you visit, the time of your visit, your browser type, and an anonymized or truncated network address. These logs are used for security and for understanding aggregate traffic patterns. They are not used to build profiles of individual visitors.</p>

        <h2>Cookies and Analytics</h2>
        <p>At launch, this site uses no analytics scripts and sets no first-party cookies for tracking. Your visit is not recorded by an analytics dashboard, and no advertising cookies are placed. A separate <a href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a> explains this in more detail, including what will change if the site is approved for an advertising program such as Google AdSense.</p>

        <h2>Third-Party Content</h2>
        <p>This site currently embeds no third-party widgets, video players, or social media feeds. Outbound links to sources and social profiles lead to other websites, each governed by its own privacy policy. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of external sites.</p>

        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>This site is a general educational publication and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the contact email, write to us and we will delete it promptly.</p>

        <h2>Data Security and Retention</h2>
        <p>Because the site collects almost nothing, there is almost nothing to protect. Emails sent to the contact address are retained only as long as needed to handle the correspondence. Server logs rotate automatically according to the hosting provider's schedule.</p>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>This policy may be updated as the site evolves, for example if an analytics tool or advertising program is added. When material changes are made, the "last updated" date at the top of this page will change, and significant changes will be noted in the cookie policy as well.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@behavioralpsychology.pro">info@behavioralpsychology.pro</a>. You can also reach us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
